==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|suster}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|swester}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*swestēr}}, from {{inh|nl|ine-pro|*swésōr}}. The sense “nurse” from the fact that (before the Reformation and in Catholic areas until recently) the majority of nurses were nuns; already in Middle Dutch generalized to lay nurses.

